%% Title: SemanticScholar Search Fallback And Batch Request Flow
%% @version 1.1.0
%% @date    2026-10-09
%% Reviewed against main 9a7339dc: semanticscholar/fetch_adapter_mixin.py, _search_fetch_flow.py and batch_request_mixin.py
%% @type    sequenceDiagram
%% @level   Provider / Interaction
%% @nodes   6
%% RULES: RULES.md §2.1, ADR-032
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant Runner as publication pipeline
    participant Adapter as SemanticScholarAdapter
    participant Search as _search_fetch_flow.py
    participant Batch as batch_request_mixin.py
    participant Fallback as fallback.py
    participant HTTP as UnifiedHTTPClient

    Runner->>Adapter: publication lookup
    alt free-text fetch without filter IDs
        Adapter->>Search: _paginate_search(query, limit)
        loop unique offsets and below 10000 pages
            Search->>HTTP: GET /paper/search
            HTTP-->>Search: raw records and next offset
            Search-->>Adapter: BronzeRecord stream
        end
    else DOI filter fetch
        Adapter->>Batch: _fetch_batch_with_nulls(DOIs)
        Batch->>HTTP: execute batch request
        HTTP-->>Batch: detailed records and unresolved IDs
        Batch-->>Adapter: BronzeRecord stream
        opt fetch_filtered_with_fallback and mapping supplied
            Adapter->>Fallback: recover unresolved DOI records by title
            Fallback-->>Adapter: fallback BronzeRecord stream
        end
    end
    Adapter-->>Runner: raw provider publication dictionaries
    Note over Search,HTTP: Repeated offset / page ceiling raises pagination-truncated error (CF-034). Absent offset or record limit ends normally.
